  "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements the first provider-execution layer on top of the canonical payment core in #331. This PR keeps provider-specific behavior behind adapters and capability gates, while adding durable operation/idempotency records and authoritative reconciliation for PlaceToPay and PayPhone.\n\nDepends on #331 and should be reviewed/merged after it.\n\nThe generated mobile contract is published separately in diegueins680/TDF-mobile#78 at commit `62dd38cfa0362d0fb880c9f0cd4933693fe77759`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds exact payment-method routing so multi-method checkouts cannot bypass a selected method.\n- Separates immutable internal order references from provider merchant references.\n- Adds `commerce_provider_operation` for durable create-operation idempotency, resource binding, outcome certainty, encrypted redirect state, and safe ambiguous-result handling.\n- Records webhook evidence as either `signature_verified` or `untrusted_callback`; evidence classification is immutable.\n- Adds hosted session create/status APIs and provider notification endpoints, including PayPhone's required `/NotificacionPago` compatibility route.\n- Implements PlaceToPay SHA-256 notification verification followed by authenticated session lookup.\n- Treats PayPhone notifications as untrusted triggers and requires an authenticated Sale lookup before changing canonical payment state.\n- Validates provider resource ID, merchant reference, amount, currency, account, environment, checkout, attempt, and intent before reconciliation.\n- Prevents fallback after an ambiguous create result, avoiding duplicate cross-provider charges.\n- Fails closed for unconfigured PlaceToPay card, bank, or DeUna payment-method identifiers and for unsupported PayPhone methods.\n- Extends admin/OpenAPI/generated web and mobile contracts with provider operation and evidence information.\n- Adds a reversible migration, production release-manifest registration, schema assertions, regression tests, and an operator verification/runbook document.\n\n## Verification completed\n\nAll results below are local/mock/database verification, not provider sandbox or staging evidence.\n\n- `stack test --fast --test-arguments='--match=provider'` \u2014 PASS, 76 examples, 0 failures.\n- `./scripts/test-provider-execution-runtime-migration.sh` \u2014 PASS against PostgreSQL 16, including double apply, encrypted redirect checks, immutable references/evidence, unsigned production callback classification, guarded rollback, operator flag preservation, and reapply.\n- `npm run test:production-release` \u2014 PASS, 60 tests, 0 failures.\n- `npm run generate:api` \u2014 PASS and deterministic (`git diff --exit-code`).\n- `npm run typecheck:ui` \u2014 PASS.\n- Mobile `npm run typecheck` \u2014 PASS at `62dd38cfa0362d0fb880c9f0cd4933693fe77759`.\n- `./scripts/test-automatic-migrations-production-schema.sh` \u2014 PASS against an isolated PostgreSQL 17/pgvector database, including manifest verification, backend health, schema verification, second-start idempotency, and unchanged migration checksum.\n- `git diff --check` \u2014 PASS.\n\nRecorded verification timestamp: 2026-09-14 09:46:43 America/Guayaquil (14:46:43 UTC).\n\n## Migration and rollback\n\n- Forward: `tdf-hq/sql/2026-09-13_provider_execution_runtime.sql`\n- Rollback: `tdf-hq/sql/rollback/2026-09-13_provider_execution_runtime_rollback.sql`\n- Release manifest ID: `2026-09-13_provider_execution_runtime`\n- Rollback intentionally refuses to remove provider operations or untrusted-callback evidence when data exists.\n- Provider notification flags are inserted conservatively; rollback removes only rows that still match the migration-owned values/reasons.\n- No production data mutation or deployment was performed.\n\n## Configuration and activation\n\nAdapters remain disabled unless the exact environment/account/configuration gates pass. Activation requires, as applicable:\n\n- PlaceToPay login, secret key, process URL, notification URL, and exact method-ID mappings for card, bank, and DeUna.\n- PayPhone bearer token, store ID, response URL, approved external-notification registration, and provider account readiness.\n- A configured application encryption key for persisted redirect/session material.\n- Explicit production account and feature-flag activation after sandbox/staging evidence and operational approval.\n\n## Known blockers and risks\n\n- No PlaceToPay or PayPhone sandbox credentials/contracts were available; no real provider sandbox transaction or callback was executed.\n- No configured staging deployment/access was exercised.\n- No live transaction, settlement, payout, or production deployment was performed.\n- Web/mobile checkout UI does not advertise these methods yet; this PR supplies the backend/runtime and generated contract needed by the dependent UI PR.\n- PlaceToPay payment links, recurring mandates, refunds, voids, captures, disputes, settlements, and payouts need separate operation/API work.\n- PayPhone's current public notification guide documents no cryptographic signature; callbacks remain untrusted until an authenticated API query confirms the payment.\n- A transport-ambiguous create response without a bound provider resource requires manual/provider-console reconciliation; automatic fallback is blocked.\n- Mixed taxable/non-taxable basket representation still requires an agreed provider tax-line strategy.\n- Marketplace connected-account, split-settlement, and seller-payout flows remain disabled unless provider contract/capability and Ecuadorian legal/accounting review establish a compliant model.\n\n## Review order\n\n1. #331 \u2014 canonical core, migrations, audit, architecture, and compatibility.\n2. This PR \u2014 provider execution, reconciliation, release registration, and generated contracts.\n3. Dependent web/mobile checkout and administration PRs.\n\n",
